   $$
   \binom{4}{2} = \frac{4!}{2!(4-2)!} = \frac{4!}{2! \cdot 2!} = \frac{24}{2 \cdot 2} = \frac{24}{4} = 6
   $$

3. **Total number of ways to choose 3 boys and 2 girls:**
   $$
   35 \times 6 = 210
   $$

The number of ways Mr. Brennan can pick the group is \boxed{210}.
